1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,380
We'd like to start our evening news bulletin with a special report.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:08,560
The weather bureau has issued a special warning regarding an approaching dust storm.

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:20,550
The unusually dry weather which we've been experiencing over the last three months has combined with strong northeasterly winds to produce a massive dust storm, which is moving steadily towards our city.

4
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:29,670
The thick clouds should hit the northwestern suburbs by about 9:00 a.m. tomorrow morning and then gradually move across the city in a southeasterly direction.

5
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:37,200
The weather bureau advises all residents to make no unnecessary trips tomorrow, as visibility will be extremely reduced.

6
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:40,820
Schools and government offices will, however, be open tomorrow.

7
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:48,680
Anyone with asthma or any other breathing disorder should remain indoors and keep doors and windows tightly closed.
